NAME
  pm crisp reverse delete-a-website - Delete A Website

SYNOPSIS
  pm crisp reverse delete-a-website [flags]

DESCRIPTION
  Delete A Website

INTENT
  reverse_etl

AVAILABILITY
  planned

OPERATION
  crisp.delete-a-website

APPROVAL
  reverse ETL plan -> preview -> explicit approval -> execute; typed destructive confirmation required

RISK
  critical

NOTES
  DELETE /v1/website/{website_id}; lane=reverse_etl_write; planned fixed Crisp operation metadata only, not a raw API escape hatch.

FLAGS
  --website-id (string): The website identifier maps_to=record.website_id
  --verify (string): User identity verification challenge (used to double-authenticate deletion) maps_to=record.verify

GLOBAL FLAGS
  --credential (string): Credential profile name; never pass token values as flags. maps_to=config.credential
  --limit (integer): Maximum PM records/items to emit when a future typed command supports pagination. maps_to=query.limit
  --json (boolean): Render machine-readable output for future implemented commands.
